Syntax: cast 'divination' <target>
        cast 'divination' <object>

Divination is an advanced form of the identify spell, revealing far more
detailed information about creatures or objects. Through careful magical
analysis, the caster perceives hidden properties, enchantments, and
characteristics that the basic identify spell cannot detect.

When cast on an object, divination reveals magical properties, charges,
bonuses, and other significant attributes. When cast on a creature, it
provides insight into their capabilities, resistances, and current status.

The accuracy and depth of information gained depends on the caster's level
and skill. Higher-level casters perceive more subtle details and are less
likely to receive erroneous readings. Even master diviners may fail to
pierce particularly powerful magical concealments.

See Also: IDENTIFY, DETECT MAGIC
